{"name":"Shrine of Pleasures","hex":"#cc3388","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shrine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A holy or sacred place dedicated to a specific deity, ancestor, hero, martyr, saint, or similar figure of awe and respect, at which said figure is venerated or worshipped.","A case, box, or receptacle, especially one in which are deposited sacred relics, as the bones of a saint."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enshrine; to place reverently, as if in a shrine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrine"},{"term":"pleasures","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of pleasure"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of pleasure"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pleasures"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shrine","blocks":[{"text":"A shrine is a sacred space dedicated to a specific deity, ancestor, hero, martyr, saint, daemon, or similar figure of respect, wherein they are venerated and/or worshipped. Shrines often contain idols, relics, or other such objects associated with the figure being venerated. A shrine at which votive offerings are made is called an altar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Gorskii_03982u.jpg/330px-Gorskii_03982u.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrine"},{"title":"Pleasures","blocks":[{"text":"Pleasures is a two-hour 1986 American television film written by Jill Gordon and directed by Sharron Miller. Its cast includes Joanna Cassidy, Barry Bostwick, Linda Purl, Rick Moses and Tracy Nelson."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pleasures"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Shrine_at_repulse_bay_to_tin_hau.jpg/500px-Shrine_at_repulse_bay_to_tin_hau.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik